From a9c4c74570508ea324aaa2f27d5f8708eb3efbac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:02:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] strongswan: apply the 6.1.0 fixes for three IKEv2 CVEs

- CVE-2026-78127: the payload enumerator leaked on a truncated log line,
  pre-authentication (encoding/message.c).
- CVE-2026-78135: CREATE_CHILD_SA was accepted on an IKE_SA that was not
  yet established, before EAP completed (task_manager_v2.c).
- CVE-2026-78133: use-after-free after a failed passive multi-KE rekeying
  collision (child_rekey, ike_rekey).

Upstream 6.1.0 fixes applied to the vendored 6.0.4 source. The IPsec
server ships off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/libcharon/encoding/message.c          | 23 ++++-----
 .../src/libcharon/sa/ikev2/task_manager_v2.c  | 34 +++++++-------
 .../libcharon/sa/ikev2/tasks/child_rekey.c    | 47 ++++++++++++++-----
 .../libcharon/sa/ikev2/tasks/child_rekey.h    |  3 +-
 .../src/libcharon/sa/ikev2/tasks/ike_rekey.c  | 40 ++++++++++++----
 .../src/libcharon/sa/ikev2/tasks/ike_rekey.h  |  3 +-
 6 files changed, 101 insertions(+), 49 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/strongswan/src/libcharon/encoding/message.c b/release/src/router/strongswan/src/libcharon/encoding/message.c
